reference_code=(APP/'src/inheritance-reference.ts').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
walk+='<section class="step"><h2>Subagent modes · reference only</h2><p>The application launches no subagents. Current docs keep a plan-mode parent restrictive despite the requested child acceptEdits setting.</p><p class="source">Source: src/inheritance-reference.ts · teaching reference, not an executed delegation</p>'+snippet(reference_code)+'</section>'

reference=[('Version-aware omitted defaults', 'The supplied slide and some SDK type comments mention auto as a possible omitted default. Current official docs say Claude Code 2.1.302+ headless/Agent SDK runs start in default unless settings or an explicit option change it. This app disables ordinary setting sources and records the actual initialization mode.'), ('Plan is not auto-approval', 'Current docs route file writes to the callback in plan mode even if a Write allow entry matches. The model may also choose not to attempt a write while planning; lack of an attempt is different from an SDK rejection. The live evidence must be read accordingly.'), ('Auto mode observations', 'Availability depends on model, provider and policy. Some actions may resolve before classifier review. The app reports actual mode, action result and any startup diagnostic without fabricating classifier reasoning or promising the same outcome on every runtime.'), ('Working-directory scope', 'acceptEdits automatically approves eligible operations in cwd or additionalDirectories. Protected paths and critical-path removals have additional rules. This app uses fixed local Read/Write operations and does not test destructive shell commands or protected system paths.'), ('Bypass still has earlier checks', 'TypeScript requires allowDangerouslySkipPermissions true. Scoped denies and hooks still apply. The live scoped Edit deny protects only the disposable result file. SDK modes are permission policy, not an operating-system sandbox.'), ('Subagent inheritance reference', 'Current docs inherit plan, acceptEdits, auto and bypass from the parent. A plan-mode parent remains restrictive even if a child definition requests acceptEdits; this differs from the supplied slide. Eligible overrides apply under default/dontAsk parents, and a child definition cannot enable bypass. This application launches no subagents.'), ('Real review versus test automation', 'The web experiment waits for an actual Approve or Reject button decision. CLI automation requires --approve-plan; the live test harness uses an explicit review callback and labels it accordingly. Only approved review can request the mode switch.'), ('Evidence and API cost', 'Nine actual SDK queries include a second model turn for the switching case. Each query has a $0.40 SDK budget threshold, not a prepaid cap. Credentials, dependencies, raw recordings and all teaching media stay outside Git.'), ('Planning artifacts versus source edits', 'The SDK planning workflow may request a Markdown plan artifact under its private configuration directory. This classroom guard blocks every extra file, including those artifacts, and logs the hook rejection separately. Do not confuse that guard rejection with the callback denying result.txt in plan mode. The actual final plan text remains reviewable.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Every architecture step has source-linked coloured code.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 29 · Permission modes\n\nFive linked student pages, large text, actual SDK experiments and coloured code in all thirteen UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson29-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson29-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson29-permission-modes`. Open http://127.0.0.1:3129 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit and model access are required. Windows may require Git Bash.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file. Enter your own model key, then restart. Existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo GitHub token or Managed Agents IDs are required. Secrets, dependencies and teaching media stay outside Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, selected lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Official SDK permissions documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/permissions)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. Run `npm test` for offline boundaries, review lifecycle, workspace and startup checks.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 29 pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')
